written out because a reader should not have to infer it.

So: fork this repository, change it, build a product on it, sell that product,
and say in plain words that your work is based on HELVE, or is compatible with
HELVE, or is a fork of HELVE. All of that is fine and none of it needs
permission. What is not fine is shipping it *as* HELVE — under the name, under
